      "writtenOn": "2023-08-17T15:26:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not sure if this is the right way to check for successful creation. It wasn\u0027t for ShaderModules. There is an `ErrorComputePipeline` object that it looks like `CreateComputePipeline` might return:\n\nhttps://osscs.corp.google.com/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/ComputePipeline.cpp;l\u003d71;drc\u003d16f579bd5f425f27c30816cac4b06508bcb3e5c8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 152,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 152,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "6ffc14d53a78299a760c1612b386adf8395bfb45",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3f1a804c_a3287a5b",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnComputePipeline.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 152,
      "author": {
        "id": 18529
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-22T19:16:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That looks like a dawn native type but Graphite interfaces with Dawn using `webgpu_cpp.h` bindings and `wgpu::ComputePipeline` should just be a wrapper around a native handle: see https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:out/Debug/gen/third_party/dawn/include/dawn/webgpu_cpp.h;drc\u003dd708cc843536cc344f0f7679a978634cc14d6153;l\u003d1019 and https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:out/Debug/gen/third_party/dawn/include/dawn/webgpu_cpp.h;l\u003d867;drc\u003dd708cc843536cc344f0f7679a978634cc14d6153. If pipeline creation failed, I would expect this to be a null handle.\n\nI\u0027m curious why this didn\u0027t work for ShaderModules. I see that `wgpu::Device` there is an alternative `CreateErrorShaderModule` method. For pipelines there are async versions that seem to return an error description (see  https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:out/Debug/gen/third_party/dawn/include/dawn/webgpu_cpp.h;l\u003d1043;drc\u003dd708cc843536cc344f0f7679a978634cc14d6153;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d1 and https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:out/Debug/gen/third_party/dawn/include/dawn/webgpu.h;drc\u003def54bf45d50e6f9990713781e788c48102639d5e;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d1;l\u003d917).\n\nMaybe we should use the async versions instead? That said if the synchronous versions don\u0027t work as intended then we should probably file bugs against Dawn. If a pipeline is invalid it shouldn\u0027t have a valid handle?",
      "parentUuid": "c6794e72_cd9e1c78",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 152,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 152,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "6ffc14d53a78299a760c1612b386adf8395bfb45",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2ae3228c_d3152cb6",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnComputePipeline.cpp",
