      "writtenOn": "2023-08-22T19:26:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For shader modules, it makes sense that a handle is returned even when compilation fails; this gives them a mechanism to return errors/warnings/info messages, rather than getting back `nullptr` if the program is bad. \n\nI don\u0027t know if the same is true of compute pipelines, but given that `ErrorComputePipeline` objects exist, I thought it was plausible.",
      "parentUuid": "3f1a804c_a3287a5b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 152,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 152,
        "endChar": 20
